      "claim": "In mice, a more distant analog [11C]12 showed very low brain-to-blood ratios, indicating poor BBB permeability and arguing against CNS access for that compound.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple structurally related molecules show direct in-vivo evidence of meaningful CNS access, including human CSF penetration, rat oral brain exposure, and PET BBB passage. The negative examples are more distant analogs and are outweighed by the closer positive evidence.",
